stages of the startup lifecycle—Idea, MVP, Launch, and Scale—for what's possible in 2026, with
the goals, exit criteria, common failure modes, and AI-powered exercises that work at each one.

In this playbook, we share:

How to validate a problem hypothesis, map a competitive landscape, and run customer discovery
with AI

Architecture, scope, and security practices that keep AI-generated MVP codebases from accruing
technical debt

A measurement framework for distinguishing genuine product-market fit from early hype

A Launch-stage operating system that replaces founder attention with agentic workflows

A product matrix for when and how to use Chat, Claude Cowork, and Claude Code across each stage
of the startup journey

Founder stories from Ambral, Anything, Carta Healthcare, HumanLayer, Vulcan Technologies, and
more

These best practices were written for founders deciding how to architect their company around AI
from day one and for the early operators helping them get there.

